cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use powerkit, please cite it as below. Please also cite the package
  that computed your power analysis (Spower, Superpower, InteractionPoweR or
  power4mome) and its method paper: powerkit's citations export
  (export_citations()) lists them for each result.
type: software
title: "powerkit: Unified Power Analysis for Psychology Designs"
version: 0.8.1
authors:
  - family-names: Thornton
    given-names: Joel
repository-code: "https://github.com/JoelThornton/Powerkit"
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
abstract: >-
  powerkit reads a single design specification for common psychology
  designs, checks that it describes a possible population, and routes it to
  established power analysis packages (Spower, Superpower, InteractionPoweR
  and power4mome) to estimate power, required sample size and sensitivity.
keywords:
  - power analysis
  - sample size
  - psychology
  - R
# Placeholder: a preferred-citation for powerkit's paper is added once that
# paper exists (and is in engine/inst/citations/refs.bib under 'powerkit').
